+    A mount can also be configured with both a high-usage threshold and a
+    low-usage threshold. A low-usage alert is useful to catch a mount that
+    normally runs busy but suddenly reports very little usage -- in
+    practice this is almost always a sign that the filesystem silently
+    failed to mount, rather than that space was genuinely freed up. To
+    configure both, use a mapping with ``high`` and/or ``low`` keys instead
+    of a plain percentage value:
+
+    .. code-block:: yaml
+
+        beacons:
+          diskusage:
+            - /: 63%
+            - /mnt/nfs:
+                high: 50%
+                low: 5%
+
+    ``high`` behaves exactly like the plain percentage form (alert when
+    usage is at or above the threshold). ``low`` alerts when usage is at or
+    below the threshold. Either key may be provided on its own.
+
     """
